# Enforce LF line endings in the working tree on every platform.
#
# WHY: this repo's shipped wire contract lives in COMMITTED byte artifacts —
# dist/error-codes.json, dist/server-route-manifest.json and
# dist/mcp-scopes.json. test/errors.test.ts, test/routeManifest.test.ts and
# test/mcp.test.ts re-derive those artifacts and compare content, and
# downstream clients vendor the JSON verbatim (e.g. phlix-ui's
# src/api/test/routeGate.api.test.ts md5-pins dist/server-route-manifest.json;
# server/hub pin this package by tag and hash their vendored copies).
# A checkout that silently rewrites LF to CRLF (git core.autocrlf=true on a
# windows runner) perturbs those bytes and poisons every hash downstream —
# the exact failure class fixed in phlix-windows-client PR #46.
#
# Census at adoption (master 35266073): 104 tracked blobs, zero CR bytes in
# any of them and no binary files — so this shield is text-only. If binary
# assets are ever added, mark them `binary` here at the same time.
* text=auto eol=lf
